infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The design writes itself from the requirements
  desc Each stated requirement forces a specific design decision — same flow, requirement-driven answer
  compares
    - label Requirement
      children
        - label 100 reads : 1 write
          desc Read-heavy access pattern
        - label Instant redirect (p99 < 50 ms)
          desc Strict tail-latency budget
        - label Codes must be short
          desc Compact identifier
        - label Redirect failure is worst
          desc Read path is the critical path
    - label Design decision
      children
        - label Cache in front of reads
          desc Hot links live in memory
        - label Precompute, never compute on hot path
          desc No slow lookup on read
        - label Counter + base-62, do not hash
          desc Avoids collisions and length
        - label Read path most replicated, write degrades first
          desc Least fragile where it matters
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
